      },
      {
        "kind": "divider",
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "kind": "container",
        "children": [
          {
            "kind": "header",
            "text": "💡 Python Concept: Variable"
          },
          {
            "kind": "write",
            "text": "Imagine you have a box."
          },
          {
            "kind": "write",
            "text": "You put something inside the box."
          },
          {
            "kind": "write",
            "text": "Then you give the box a name."
          },
          {
            "kind": "write",
            "text": "Later, you can use that name to find what you stored."
          },
          {
            "kind": "success",
            "text": "In Python, this named storage is called a VARIABLE."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "container",
        "children": [
          {
            "kind": "write",
            "text": "🥭 Dabbo remembers:"
          },
          {
            "kind": "metric",
            "label": "Mangoes",
            "value": "50"
          },
          {
            "kind": "write",
            "text": "The important idea is:"
          },
          {
            "kind": "info",
            "text": "A variable is simply a name that helps Python remember a value."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    [
